for over a thousand years britain has  had a royal family today we have the  windsors but who exactly are they  [Music]  the lineage of the royal family can  pretty much be traced back to william  the conqueror in 1066.  since then almost every successive king  or queen has had some sort of relation  to him went through blood or marriage  but it wasn't until 1917 the family took  the name windsor before then the royals  were known by their house names so the  tudors and the stewards for example but  during the first world war king george v  wanted to distance himself from his  german relatives so the house of saks  coburg gotha became the house of windsor  by far the most famous windsor is queen  elizabeth ii  she is the longest reigning monarch the  country has ever had she has four  children charles ann andrew and edward  my lord pray be seated  prince charles is next in line for the  throne and his mother's longevity has  made him the longest and oldest serving  heir apparent  in british history  prince william is third in line to the  throne he and his wife catherine are  among the most popular royals with the  public  prince harry and megan are two more  extremely well-known members of the  family but the mexican spat with the  firm saw them step away from royal life  in total the queen has eight  grandchildren and twelve  great-grandchildren  so good it's quite a quite a gathering  [Music]  the royal family is large and while many  of them are recognized around the world  and seen as senior royals the line of  succession is long and contains some  names you may not have heard of  aside from the top tier of royals there  are some famous faces like princess  beatrice and princess eugenie but also  perhaps less well-known ones like prince  michael who is one of over 30 cousins  that the queen has a fun fact about  michael is that when he was born in 1942  he was seventh in line to the throne now  he's been relegated all the way down to  50 seconds somebody else can do the  rest of it  there are also a number of royal family  members who do not have an official  title probably the most well-known royal  in this category is the former olympic  equestrian zara tindall archie and  lillabet harry and megan's children also  don't have titles but that could change  when prince charles becomes king when  they could qualify for hrh status of  course a lot though depends on how much  harry and megan are involved in the  family at that stage lillabet who is the  queen's 11th grandchild and 8th in line  to the throne is also the most senior  royal to have dual us uk citizenship  the members of the royal family who work  full time for the queen are funded by  something called the sovereign grant as  well as her majesty's personal wealth  and her portfolio as sovereign the  government-funded portion the sovereign  grant also covers the maintenance of the  occupied royal palaces and therefore the  homes of the senior royals lucky enough  to live in them  prince charles as the prince of wales is  slightly different he earns money from  the duchy of cornwall a large area of  land mainly in the southwest of england  the prince uses part of this income to  meet the costs of his private life and  those of his wife the duchess of  cornwall as well as his sons prince  william and prince harry however many  royals choose to work normal jobs 10th  in line to the throne princess beatrice  is vice president of a software company  her sister princess eugenie runs an art  gallery and peter phillips who is the  queen's oldest grandson through his  mother anne runs a sports and  entertainment company  and most famously since stepping away  from royal duties prince harry has  started working for a start-up and also  announced that him and megan are going  to appear in a netflix series  the british royal family is sprawling to  say the least but the future and size of  the british monarchy will depend upon  the youngest senior royals and the  decisions that are made after the reign  of queen elizabeth comes to an end  [Music]
 

